{
  "step_1": "The decision reason is applicable to the decision problem because both lotteries have well-defined monetary outcomes and probabilities. Lottery A offers a sure outcome of 500 Euros (100% probability). Lottery B offers two outcomes: 1000 Euros (50% probability) and 0 Euros (50% probability). The reason focuses on identifying the minimum absolute value outcome (which is 0 Euros in Lottery B), treating the sure outcome (500 Euros) as a reference point, and then evaluating the differences between the sure outcome and the other outcomes (1000 and 0), weighted by their probabilities. The sum of the sure outcome and the weighted differences is computed for each lottery, and the one with the higher sum is preferred. This calculation is feasible given the available data.",
